Auto-run hipification before CMake configuration

When ROCm is detected, the build system now automatically runs
tools/amd_build/build_amd.py before CMake configuration. This fixes
the --cmake-only workflow (and the normal setup.py build path) so
users no longer need to manually hipify sources before building.

ROCm detection mirrors cmake/public/LoadHIP.cmake: ROCM_PATH env var,
rocm-sdk CLI, CMakeUserPresets.json, then /opt/rocm as fallback.
Hipification is skipped if the output files already exist.

